      "prediction": {
        "kind": "removal",
        "band": {
          "low": 12,
          "high": 26.606
        },
        "text": "The algebra predicts that the Service has no ready endpoint, and that the rules of each node have no backend. The band is 12 s to 26.606 s after the fault. Redis is black-holed for each replica for the hold (27 s). Each request needs Redis, thus each request fails from the fault until the callers recover. Before the readiness latch of a replica trips (8 s–20 s), each request on it waits for Redis and fails slowly. Then its controller is not ready, and the service refuses each request at once with a 503. The kubelet and the propagation (Cilium 1.20.4 sources: the reflector buffer (500 ms) and the BPF reconciler (1 ms), plus the shared path of CAL.T07.iptables (0.105 s)) remove both replicas 12 s–26.606 s after the fault. Then the Service is empty, and its rules refuse each new connection. The lame duck closes each connection after the trip, thus each next request opens a new connection, and the empty Service refuses it. After the heal, the client of Redis connects again in 3.1 s at the most, and the readiness of the service recovers up to 6 s later. The kubelet then finds a replica ready in 2 s at the most, and the propagation adds it to the rules. Each client sends a request each 20 ms, thus about 3954–6135 requests fail."
      },
